  "output": {
    "answer": "No, a passed gate doesn't merge itself. The checklist calls for a stronger model to review each lane first, naming what it actually checked — re-running the gate's command, spot-checking specific claims, diffing against the contract, not just \"looks good.\" Only after that review does the merge happen, with `merge --no-ff` and a commit body stating what was learned. The unattended-run diagram shows the same order: a cleared gate unlocks the next lane, but only a cleared and reviewed gate reaches me for the production flip or merge decision. So review comes before landing, not after.",
